# TypeScript Standards

- `strict` TypeScript only; no `any` unless justified at a true boundary and typed immediately
- Prefer explicit domain types in `packages/*` over duplicating shapes in services
- Public APIs must be documented
- No raw SQL — Prisma only
- No distributed prompts — load from `prompts/`
- Prefer dependency injection and ports/adapters over concrete imports in domain layers
- ESLint + Prettier must pass; do not disable rules without an ADR or documented exception
